 "topic": "What if GTA6 cheat codes worked in real life?",
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "p1",
   "text": "There's no chime this time. Just silence."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p2",
   "text": "Ellie's voice stops halfway through your name. The man's hand stops on the door handle. Outside, a bird hangs in the air, wings wide open, not moving."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p3",
   "text": "The whole world is paused. Everything except you."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p4",
   "text": "In front of your face, in the same glowing letters: Game paused."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p5",
   "text": "Then, across the street, a front door opens. Someone walks out into the frozen evening, holding a controller exactly like yours."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p6",
   "text": "They look up at your window. And they wave."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p7",
   "text": "Who else has a controller? How long have they had it? And what happens when someone presses play?"
  },
  {
   "beat": "p8",
   "text": "Is any of this real? The cheats aren't. But every catch is. People born without pain really do get hurt without noticing. Every dollar bill really does have its own serial number. One car made from nothing would cost a fifth of the world's energy for a year. And pilots really did see a jetpack next to their plane."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p9",
   "text": "So which cheat would you have entered first? Tell me in the comments. And this one's part of our series about video games in real life. The next one's right here."
  }
 ],
